<title>ITALY: Italy VAT rises not inflationary - Visco.</title>
<headline>Italy VAT rises not inflationary - Visco.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italy's Finance Minister Vincenzo Visco said increases in value added tax in the 1998 budget would only have a one-off effect on prices and would not be inflationary.</p>
<p>&quot;There will be some effect on prices but it is not inflation. It's a one-off effect on prices,&quot; Visco told a news conference after the cabinet approved a three-year economic strategy, known as the DPEF.</p>
<p>The DPEF outlines the government's taxing and spending targets for the next three years.</p>
</text>
